{
 "voice": "recorded",
 "speaker": "a real person (credit pending her confirmation)",
 "speed": null,
 "lang": "en-us",
 "style": "whisper",
 "source": "voice-evelyn/evelyn-s3-full.m4a",
 "made_by": "polish.py --style whisper on the whole recording, cut by word alignment (set/s3_cut.py)",
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "beat": "hook",
   "text": "Your skin is still healing after it looks healed.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "01.wav",
   "dur": 2.81,
   "sha256": "0eab300ef3c347ef90da2d66180b2dd0e08ba862f3c92c066a8299000377e692"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "beat": "normal",
   "text": "When a small gap in your skin closes, it looks finished in a week or two, but it isn't.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "02.wav",
   "dur": 6.87,
   "sha256": "95252a7b1b40026ac6b3fbb0006e1ff3ed0ea8cf965600eed4c8e6c5820df762"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "beat": "change",
   "text": "Underneath, the work has already begun.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "03.wav",
   "dur": 3.49,
   "sha256": "74a570de8dc7a0efcd27b0e21850b541e4650b949009a0d3b1e459170f265871"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "beat": "why",
   "text": "First, your body seals it and calls in its cleaning crews.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "04.wav",
   "dur": 5.49,
   "sha256": "5c92675848c0dabfe8f270df749e72c0b19c15084b4202508070779eacbcdfd1"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "beat": "why",
   "text": "New cells creep in from the edges, and repair cells lay down fresh collagen.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "05.wav",
   "dur": 6.53,
   "sha256": "a3371b06f4a72684327202dbdb5badda0c5e44e6105a32f7d8ed02433615ce5c"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "beat": "whoa",
   "text": "Quickly, a little messily, like scaffolding.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "06.wav",
   "dur": 5.51,
   "sha256": "b21fe4e774d989a50b53acc56aa070aad14647d7cae1a2a7de08eca753cbca4e"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "beat": "whoa",
   "text": "But for months, sometimes a year or more, the skin keeps quietly rebuilding.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "07.wav",
   "dur": 7.27,
   "sha256": "fe60a8f4a9cb75f0e0fe159e28a573b1a4eec69549046213662588088401bba1"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "beat": "takeaway",
   "text": "Then, quick collagen is traded for stronger fibers drawn slowly into line. The spot grows flatter and softer, paler.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "08.wav",
   "dur": 10.38,
   "sha256": "ad33e7c6ad86de18179420e122e38633add75cadce42909330813ddb8391f24b"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo09",
   "beat": "takeaway",
   "text": "Even then, rebuilt skin usually ends up at most around eighty percent as strong as before.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "09.wav",
   "dur": 7.61,
   "sha256": "3caa8cedd3727d032fa9a4345330088ee7ab71853ce43a2a68149aedd1fcdd60"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo10",
   "beat": "takeaway",
   "text": "So the skin you think of as healed is still being gently rewoven, long after you've forgotten it.",
   "stars": [],
   "phonemes": null,
   "file": "10.wav",
   "dur": 8.49,
   "sha256": "5944c328b5edce5199f77e20b7e5ef8262def9e4c760d1f9e2caf20eb72e6e57"
  }
 ]
}